      "description": "Chip's Jack Machine is a pocket-sized classic house drum machine — 16 voices, a 16/32-step sequencer, and the hands-on knob-per-function workflow of the original hardware, with no menus to dig through.\n\nMost of the kit is synthesized live rather than played back from a sample library, so every knob genuinely reshapes the sound instead of filtering a recording. A few voices are built from recordings where a real one simply sounded better.\n\nFEATURES\n\n• 16 voices — bass drum, snare, low/mid/hi tom, clap, closed and open hat, cowbell, rim shot, maracas, low/mid/high conga, claves, and cymbal.\n• Per-voice TUNE, DECAY, TONE, SNAPPY, LEVEL, PAN and VERB — every one of them live.\n• 4 scenes (A/B/C/D) with instant switching, copy and paste. Each scene keeps its own pattern, bar length, mute/solo state and knob settings.\n• 8, 16 or 32-step patterns with swing.\n• Step recording — arm RECORD and play the pads in.\n• Load your own audio into any voice with SAMPLE.\n• Low-latency audio engine built for playing, not just playback.\n• Export a pattern as WAV, or export every voice separately as stems.\n• Save and load projects as .house files and move them between your devices — the same format the whole Architect Series uses.\n\nRuns on iPhone and iPad.\n\nBuy it once and it's yours. No subscription, no account, no ads, no in-app purchases, and no network connection — the app works entirely offline, forever.\n\nPart of the Time2Jack Architect Series.",
